\title{sisHMRF: Spatial Immune State Inference via Hidden Markov Random Fields}
\description{
Continuous-latent-variable hidden Markov random field for inferring immune state landscapes from spatial transcriptomics data. Unlike discrete-domain HMRF methods (BayesSpace, SC-MEB) that partition tissue into sharp clusters, sisHMRF models immune archetypes as continuous latent variables under a Gaussian Markov random field (GMRF) prior. The package provides variational EM inference, spatial feature construction from curated immune gene sets, immune activation and suppression scoring (IAS / ISS / IBI), and publication-quality visualization of continuous spatial gradients, boundary zones, and immune archetypes. Designed for 10x Visium, Xenium, MERFISH, and other spatial transcriptomics platforms.
}
